  s0462: ["In Yanhe year 2, Defender-General Prince of Le'an Fan was Governor of Yongzhou; edict had Shi and Vice Director of Secretariat Gao Yun both as consulting staff officers.", "In Yanhe 2 Prince of Le'an Fan, Defender-General, was Governor of Yong; Shi and Secretariat Vice Director Gao Yun were made his consulting officers."],
  s0463: ["He declined and was excused.", "He declined and was excused."],
  s0464: ["Shi was serene and loved the Way, broadly read records and transmissions, especially fond of glossing the Cangjie and Erya.", "Shi was serene, loved the Way, read widely, especially glossing Cangjie and Erya."],
  s0465: ["He composed \"Explanation of Characters\" but did not finish.", "He wrote \"Explanation of Characters\" but did not finish."],
  s0466: ["In the second year of Yitai'an he died, posthumously Governor of Yuzhou, posthumous name Marquis Su.", "In Yitai'an 2 he died, posthumously Governor of Yuzhou, posthumous name Marquis Su."],
  s0467: ["Son Ji inherited the father's title, post of Administrator of Wei commandery, government with a pure reputation.", "Son Ji inherited, was Administrator of Wei commandery, famed for pure rule."],
  s0468: ["Added title General Who Pacifies the Distance.", "He was given supernumerary rank General Who Pacifies the Distance."],
  s0469: ["When Prince of Song Liu Chang opened his headquarters, Ji was summoned as consulting staff officer.", "When Prince of Song Liu Chang opened headquarters Ji was summoned as consulting officer."],
  s0470: ["Mao Xiuzhi, styled Jingwen, native of Yangwu in Xingyang.", "Mao Xiuzhi, styled Jingwen, of Yangwu in Xingyang."],
  s0471: ["For generations the house served Jin.", "His house served Jin for generations."],
  s0472: ["When Liu Yu pacified Guanzhong he left his son Yizhen to garrison Chang'an, making Xiuzhi marshal.", "When Liu Yu pacified Guanzhong he left son Yizhen at Chang'an with Xiuzhi as marshal."],
  s0473: ["When Yizhen was defeated Xiuzhi was taken at Tongwan.", "When Yizhen fell Xiuzhi was taken at Tongwan."],
  s0474: ["When Taiwu pacified Helian Chang he obtained him.", "Taiwu pacified Helian Chang and took him."],
  s0475: ["He was made to lead Wu troops; for merit enfeoffed General of Wu Troops.", "He was set to lead Wu troops and enfeoffed General of Wu Troops for merit."],
  s0476: ["Xiuzhi could make southern food and personally season it, often to satisfaction.", "Xiuzhi could cook southern food and season it himself to please."],
  s0477: ["Taiwu personally favored him, repeatedly promoted to Vice Director of Masters of Writing, enfeoffed Duke of Nan commandery, constantly in the Imperial Kitchen directing imperial meals.", "Taiwu favored him, raised him to Vice Director, Duke of Nan, always in the Imperial Kitchen directing meals."],
  s0478: ["On campaign against Helong, when the armies besieged the city the traveling palace had few men; Song's old general Zhu Xiuzhi was General of Yunzhong and wished to lead Wu troops in revolt.", "Besieging Helong the camp had few men; Song's Zhu Xiuzhi, General of Yunzhong, wished to lead Wu troops in revolt."],
  s0479: ["He entered Helong hoping to float south by sea and return.", "He entered Helong hoping to sail south by sea."],
  s0480: ["He told Xiuzhi; Xiuzhi would not listen and he stopped.", "He told Xiuzhi; Xiuzhi refused and he stopped."],
  s0481: ["That day without Xiuzhi a great upheaval nearly happened.", "That day without Xiuzhi a great disaster nearly came."],
  s0482: ["Zhu Xiuzhi then fled to Feng Hong.", "Zhu Xiuzhi fled to Feng Hong."],
  s0483: ["Xiuzhi again for military merit was promoted Special Advancement, General Who Pacifies the Army, rank below Cui Hao.", "Xiuzhi rose again for merit to Special Advancement, General Who Pacifies the Army, below Cui Hao."],
  s0484: ["Hao because he was an old house of China, though not broadly versed still dipped into books and records, and debated with him.", "Hao, because he was an old Chinese house, though not broad still read books and debated with him."],
  s0485: ["Next they reached Chen Shou's \"Records of the Three Kingdoms\"; he said \"it has the air of an ancient good historian; what he wrote is canonical in meaning — since Ban Gu none match Shou.\"", "They came to Chen Shou's \"Records of the Three Kingdoms\"; Hao said it had the air of a good ancient historian, canonical since Ban Gu."],
  s0486: ["Xiuzhi said: \"In Shu I once heard elders say Shou had been a clerk under Zhuge Liang and was flogged a hundred strokes, so in judging the Martial Lord he wrote: adapting to change was not his strength.\"", "Xiuzhi said, \"In Shu elders said Shou had been Zhuge Liang's clerk, was flogged a hundred times, so he wrote the Martial Lord was weak at adaptation.\""],
  s0487: ["Hao then argued: \"Chen Shou's judgment of Liang was praise beyond measure from old obligation, not words of resentment.\"", "Hao argued, \"Shou's judgment of Liang was old obligation praising too much, not resentment.\""],
  s0488: ["Liang's serving Bei was the time when hero and lord met; ruler and minister matched, fish and water as metaphor.", "Liang serving Bei was hero and lord meeting, ruler and minister like fish and water."],
  s0489: ["Yet he could not contend with Cao for the realm, abandoned Jingzhou, retreated into Ba-Shu, held poor rugged ground, styled himself emperor among border barbarians — this is the lowest stratagem.", "Yet he could not fight Cao for the realm, abandoned Jingzhou, retreated to Ba-Shu, held poor hills, styled himself emperor among barbarians—the lowest stratagem."],
  s0490: ["He may be paired with Zhao Tuo, yet to rank with Guan Zhong and Xiao He — is that not excessive!", "He may match Zhao Tuo; to rank with Guan Zhong and Xiao He—is that not too much!"],
  s0491: ["Moreover Liang held Shu, did not measure strength, used harsh law to control Shu men, wished with border barbarians' masses to resist the central state.", "Moreover Liang held Shu, misread strength, ruled Shu with harsh law, wished border tribes to resist the center."],
  s0492: ["He sent troops out Longyou, twice attacked Qishan, once attacked Chencang, slow and missing the moment, broken and returned.", "He marched from Longyou, twice attacked Qishan, once Chencang, slow and late, broken and back."],
  s0493: ["Later he entered Qin River valley and again sought field battle.", "Later he entered Qinchuan and again sought battle in the open."],
  s0494: ["The Wei men knew his intent and wore him down without fighting.", "Wei knew his mind and wore him down without fighting."],
  s0495: ["Wits exhausted, power spent, he fell ill and died.", "Wits gone, power spent, he fell ill and died."],
  s0496: ["By this speaking, how does he fit an ancient good general who sees difficulty and knows when to stop?", "By that measure, how is he an ancient good general who sees difficulty and stops?"],
  s0497: ["Xiuzhi said Hao's words were right.", "Xiuzhi said Hao was right."],
  s0498: ["Later he died as Grand Director of the Outer Capital Kitchen, posthumous name Duke Gong.", "Later he died as Grand Director of the Outer Capital Kitchen, posthumous Duke Gong."],
  s0499: ["Xiuzhi in the south had four sons; only son Faren entered Wei.", "In the south Xiuzhi had four sons; only Faren entered Wei."],
